course: dictionary
lesson: 9416
title: Squeeze: pressing, fitting and holding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Squeeze is a word with more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «Squeeze a lemon» means press it hard, while «squeeze into the car» means push yourself into a small space. The clues tell you which meaning is right.
explain: Look for the pressure in the sentence. «The inner core stays solid despite the heat because the enormous pressure of everything above squeezes it.» The word pressure is the clue, so squeezes means pushes hard from all sides. Swap in press and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Squeeze can be a verb or a noun. In «squeeze someone's hand», it is a doing word: you press gently to show love or comfort. In «a squeeze of lemon», it is a naming word: the small amount you get by pressing. In «a tight squeeze», it means a space that is almost too small.
fact: Squeeze means to press something hard, often from the sides.
fact: Squeeze can also mean to push yourself or something into a small space.
fact: «A tight squeeze» means a space that is almost too small.
fact: «Squeeze someone's hand» means to press it gently to show love or comfort.
fact: Squeeze is a verb (squeeze, squeezes, squeezed, squeezing) and also a noun (a squeeze).
exercise: «Leo tried to squeeze into the gap between the boxes.» What does squeeze mean here? | Press something hard to get juice out | Run very fast | Hold someone's hand gently | *Push yourself into a small space
exercise: «Mum gave my hand a gentle squeeze.» What does the squeeze show? | Anger | *Love or comfort | Tiredness | Hunger
exercise: «Add a squeeze of lemon to the tea.» What is a squeeze of lemon? | A type of fish | *A small amount got by pressing | A loud noise | A large space
test: «The gap in the crowd was a tight squeeze.» What does a tight squeeze mean? | Lots of empty room | A kind of hug from a friend | *A space that is almost too small | A very loud crowd
test: «When a crowd pushes, move to the side towards space; a crowd squeezing too tightly can crush people.» What is the safe action? | Hold tight to the nearest person | Push harder into the middle | Stand still and close your eyes | *Move to the side towards space
exam: «Its strong walls resist the squeeze of deep water.» What does squeeze mean here? | A small drink of juice | A hug from a diver | A narrow tunnel | *The pressing force of deep water
